{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This page covers common Svelte and TypeScript problems when using TanStack\nForm."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"an-input-does-not-start-with-the-expected-value","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An input does not start with the expected value"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every value rendered by an input should exist in form-level "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultValues"},{"type":"text","value":"\nwhen the form is created."}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { createForm } from '@tanstack/svelte-form'\n\n  const form = createForm(() => ({\n    defaultValues: {\n      firstName: '',\n      subscribed: false,\n    },\n  }))\n</script>","lang":"svelte"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Do not omit "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultValues"},{"type":"text","value":" or rely on a field-level default. When values come\nfrom an API, render a loading state before mounting the editable form or supply\na complete fallback shape."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"a-field-value-is-unknown","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A field value is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unknown"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Field names and values are inferred from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultValues"},{"type":"text","value":". Check that you have\nnot widened the initial object to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Record<string, unknown>"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"any"},{"type":"text","value":", or an\nunrelated union. Prefer a concrete value type:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { createForm } from '@tanstack/svelte-form'\n\n  type Profile = { firstName: string; age: number }\n\n  const defaults: Profile = { firstName: '', age: 0 }\n  const form = createForm(() => ({ defaultValues: defaults }))\n</script>","lang":"svelte"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For extremely large forms, split UI into typed components or scoped form and\nfield groups instead of casting each field value."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-instantiation-is-excessively-deep","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type instantiation is excessively deep"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This TypeScript error usually involves a very large recursive value shape, a\nwidely inferred union, or an unsupported composition. Reduce it to the smallest\nform that reproduces the problem, keep "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultValues"},{"type":"text","value":" concrete, and avoid\nunnecessary generic wrappers."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the minimal reproduction still fails, report it in the\n"},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/form/issues","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Form issue tracker"}]},{"type":"text","value":". Include\nthe TypeScript and Svelte versions, the form value type, and the smallest\nfailing field."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"errors-exist-but-are-not-displayed","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Errors exist but are not displayed"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.errors"},{"type":"text","value":" respects the form's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"errorVisibility"},{"type":"text","value":" policy. Inspect\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.meta.original.errors"},{"type":"text","value":" when debugging whether validation ran but the\nissues are intentionally hidden. Also confirm that the input calls\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.handleBlur"},{"type":"text","value":" if the policy depends on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isBlurred"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"an-input-does-not-start-with-the-expected-value","text":"An input does not start with the expected value","level":2},{"id":"a-field-value-is-unknown","text":"A field value is unknown","level":2},{"id":"type-instantiation-is-excessively-deep","text":"Type instantiation is excessively deep","level":2},{"id":"errors-exist-but-are-not-displayed","text":"Errors exist but are not displayed","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThis page covers common Svelte and TypeScript problems when using TanStack\nForm.\n\n## An input does not start with the expected value\n\nEvery value rendered by an input should exist in form-level `defaultValues`\nwhen the form is created.\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { createForm } from '@tanstack/svelte-form'\n\n  const form = createForm(() => ({\n    defaultValues: {\n      firstName: '',\n      subscribed: false,\n    },\n  }))\n</script>\n```\n\nDo not omit `defaultValues` or rely on a field-level default. When values come\nfrom an API, render a loading state before mounting the editable form or supply\na complete fallback shape.\n\n## A field value is `unknown`\n\nField names and values are inferred from `defaultValues`. Check that you have\nnot widened the initial object to `Record<string, unknown>`, `any`, or an\nunrelated union. Prefer a concrete value type:\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { createForm } from '@tanstack/svelte-form'\n\n  type Profile = { firstName: string; age: number }\n\n  const defaults: Profile = { firstName: '', age: 0 }\n  const form = createForm(() => ({ defaultValues: defaults }))\n</script>\n```\n\nFor extremely large forms, split UI into typed components or scoped form and\nfield groups instead of casting each field value.\n\n## Type instantiation is excessively deep\n\nThis TypeScript error usually involves a very large recursive value shape, a\nwidely inferred union, or an unsupported composition. Reduce it to the smallest\nform that reproduces the problem, keep `defaultValues` concrete, and avoid\nunnecessary generic wrappers.\n\nIf the minimal reproduction still fails, report it in the\n[TanStack Form issue tracker](https://github.com/TanStack/form/issues). Include\nthe TypeScript and Svelte versions, the form value type, and the smallest\nfailing field.\n\n## Errors exist but are not displayed\n\n`field.errors` respects the form's `errorVisibility` policy. Inspect\n`field.meta.original.errors` when debugging whether validation ran but the\nissues are intentionally hidden. Also confirm that the input calls\n`field.handleBlur` if the policy depends on `isBlurred`.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: debugging\ntitle: Debugging Svelte Usage\n---\n\nThis page covers common Svelte and TypeScript problems when using TanStack\nForm.\n\n## An input does not start with the expected value\n\nEvery value rendered by an input should exist in form-level `defaultValues`\nwhen the form is created.\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { createForm } from '@tanstack/svelte-form'\n\n  const form = createForm(() => ({\n    defaultValues: {\n      firstName: '',\n      subscribed: false,\n    },\n  }))\n</script>\n```\n\nDo not omit `defaultValues` or rely on a field-level default. When values come\nfrom an API, render a loading state before mounting the editable form or supply\na complete fallback shape.\n\n## A field value is `unknown`\n\nField names and values are inferred from `defaultValues`. Check that you have\nnot widened the initial object to `Record<string, unknown>`, `any`, or an\nunrelated union. Prefer a concrete value type:\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { createForm } from '@tanstack/svelte-form'\n\n  type Profile = { firstName: string; age: number }\n\n  const defaults: Profile = { firstName: '', age: 0 }\n  const form = createForm(() => ({ defaultValues: defaults }))\n</script>\n```\n\nFor extremely large forms, split UI into typed components or scoped form and\nfield groups instead of casting each field value.\n\n## Type instantiation is excessively deep\n\nThis TypeScript error usually involves a very large recursive value shape, a\nwidely inferred union, or an unsupported composition. Reduce it to the smallest\nform that reproduces the problem, keep `defaultValues` concrete, and avoid\nunnecessary generic wrappers.\n\nIf the minimal reproduction still fails, report it in the\n[TanStack Form issue tracker](https://github.com/TanStack/form/issues). Include\nthe TypeScript and Svelte versions, the form value type, and the smallest\nfailing field.\n\n## Errors exist but are not displayed\n\n`field.errors` respects the form's `errorVisibility` policy. Inspect\n`field.meta.original.errors` when debugging whether validation ran but the\nissues are intentionally hidden. Also confirm that the input calls\n`field.handleBlur` if the policy depends on `isBlurred`.\n"}
